{"tool_name":"enimpute","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"EnImpute","home":"https://github.com/Zhangxf-ccnu/EnImpute","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"R package for imputing dropout events in single cell RNA sequencing data via ensemble learning.","addition_date":"2019-08-09T13:07:07Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:25Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:EnImpute","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"zhangxf@mail.ccnu.edu.cn","name":"Xiao-Fei Zhang","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/Zhangxf-ccnu/EnImpute/blob/master/EnImpute-manual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Imputation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3557"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"EnImpute","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"hans","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTZ435","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 The Author(s). All rights reserved.Imputation of dropout events that may mislead downstream analyses is a key step in analyzing single-cell RNA-sequencing (scRNA-seq) data. We develop EnImpute, an R package that introduces an ensemble learning method for imputing dropout events in scRNA-seq data. EnImpute combines the results obtained from multiple imputation methods to generate a more accurate result. A Shiny application is developed to provide easier implementation and visualization. Experiment results show that EnImpute outperforms the individual state-of-the-art methods in almost all situations. EnImpute is useful for correcting the noisy scRNA-seq data before performing downstream analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Hu X."},{"name":"Ou-Yang L."},{"name":"Yan H."},{"name":"Yang S."},{"name":"Zhang X.-F."},{"name":"Zhao X.-M."}],"citationCount":5,"date"